"# Getting started\n\nNodus is a component library for [Reef.js](https://reefjs.com) 13. Every component is a **function\nthat returns an HTML string**; interactive components also get a *behavior* that initializes\nitself. No build step is needed in development: ES modules and an *import map* are enough.\n\n## Pick your starting point\n\n| Situation | Path |\n|---|---|\n| New application | The **starter** generates a complete application (build, tests, Nodus updates): [Create an application](../../../STARTER.md) |\n| Existing application | Copy Nodus' `dist/` and declare an import map — this page |\n| Existing application, moving to the starter | [Migrate an application](../../../MIGRATION.md) |\n\n## 1. Get Nodus and Reef\n\nIn the Nodus repository, `npm install` then `npm run build` produce `dist/`. Copy that folder\n**as a whole** into your project (for instance `libs/nodus/dist/`), after emptying the previous\ncopy: a file removed between two versions must not survive in your project. Copy Reef 13 too\n(`node_modules/reefjs/dist/reef.es.min.js`) so you depend on no CDN.\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nrm -rf ../my-project/libs/nodus/dist && cp -R dist ../my-project/libs/nodus/dist\n```\n\n## 2. A minimal page\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n  <script type=\"importmap\">\n  {\n    \"imports\": {\n      \"reefjs\": \"./vendor/reef/reef.es.min.js\",\n      \"nodus\": \"./libs/nodus/dist/index.js\",\n      \"nodus/\": \"./libs/nodus/dist/\"\n    }\n  }\n  </script>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"./libs/nodus/dist/nodus.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"app\"></div>\n  <script type=\"module\" src=\"./app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n```js\n// app.js\nimport { signal, component } from 'reefjs';\nimport { Button, Field, Input, Dialog, DialogTrigger, escapeHtml, setStrings, stringsEn } from 'nodus';\nimport 'nodus/reef/reef-init.js'; // registers the behaviors (Dialog…)\n\nsetStrings(stringsEn); // default labels in English (Close, Copy…) — French otherwise\n\nconst state = signal({ name: '' });\n\nfunction view() {\n  return `\n    ${Field({ id: 'name', label: 'Your name', children:\n      Input({ id: 'name', value: state.name, sync: true, attrs: { 'data-input': 'name' } }) })}\n    <p>Hello ${escapeHtml(state.name || '…')}!</p>\n    ${DialogTrigger({ dialogId: 'about', children: Button({ label: 'About' }) })}\n    ${Dialog({ id: 'about', title: 'About', children: '<p>Built with Reef and Nodus.</p>' })}`;\n}\n\n// A single delegated listener: Reef strips on* attributes from templates.\ndocument.addEventListener('input', e => {\n  if (e.target.matches('[data-input=\"name\"]')) state.name = e.target.value;\n});\n\ncomponent('#app', view);\n```\n\nServe the folder with any static server (`npx serve .`) and open the page: the field follows the\nstate, the dialog opens, traps focus and closes with Escape.\n\n## 3. Five rules to know right away\n\n1. **`props` or `attrs`.** An unknown prop is silently ignored: `Input({ label })` does not exist,\n   a field gets its label from `Field`. HTML attributes go through `attrs`.\n   See [props vs attrs](../../../GUIDELINES.md#1-composants-nodus--props-vs-attrs) (in French).\n2. **Escape data.** Text props accept HTML: user input or fetched data goes through `escapeHtml()`.\n3. **Delegate events.** One listener per type on `document`, never an `onclick` in a template.\n   See [event delegation](../../../GUIDELINES.md#2-event-delegation--une-architecture-pas-des-handlers-inline) (in French).\n4. **`sync: true`** on a field whose state is the source of truth: Reef reapplies the value on every render.\n5. **An interactive component's content is frozen** (`reef-ignore`): to make it follow the state, use\n   its controlled mode or `registry.remount()`.\n\n## 4. Theme, customization, language\n\n- **Theme**: light or dark following the system; `data-theme=\"dark\"` or `\"light\"` on `<html>`\n  forces it.\n- **Customize**: redefining the semantic tokens (and their dark value) themes the whole library —\n  see [Colors and surfaces](#/foundations/colors).\n- **Language** of default labels: `setStrings(stringsEn)` before the first render, as above;\n  `setStrings(stringsFr)` to switch back.\n\n## 5. Slimming the bundle\n\n`reef-init.js` registers every behavior. In production, register only the ones you use: the\n**Import** section of each component page gives the exact code (ADR-002). CSS works the same way:\n`base.css` plus `components/<name>.css` (ADR-003).\n\n## Next\n\n- [Components](#/components): preview, playground, API and accessibility for each one.\n- [Conventions and Reef pitfalls](../../../GUIDELINES.md) (in French): forms, lists, reactive islands.\n- [Demos](../../../demos/): twelve complete applications.\n"